            <creation xml:id="creation_id1a88390b">
               <date enddate="1855-05-27" startdate="1851-04-10" xml:id="date_611806b7">10 Apr. 1851 to 27 May 1855</date>
               <geogName xml:id="geogName_idbb31bd0c"/>
            </creation>
            <history xml:id="history_id4cd37647">
               <p xml:id="idm128">Sophie Gade was born on 28 May 1831 as the first child of J.P.E. Hartmann and his wife Emma, who was a composer in her own right. Like all Hartmann's children she got a thorough musical education. Gade had know her since she was a child and dedicated the three first of  his "Bilder des Orients" to her on the occasion of her 19th birthday. Less than a year later on 9 April 1851 they got engaged and the marriage took place on 27 April the following year. They were married at Garnisons Kirke, where Gade was organist, as his father-in-law had been until 1843. On 20 May 1855 Sophie gave birth to the twins Felix and Emma but died on 15 June apparently as the consequence of a fall.</p>
            </history>
