            <physDesc xml:id="physDesc_bf5fc484">
               <titlePage label="" xml:id="titlePage_ffea2b08">
                  <p xml:id="idm69">Calender / eller: / Mærke- og Mindedage / for / Sophie. / Observerede og optegnede / af [Gade's musical signature] / 1855 / Kjøbenhavn.</p>
               </titlePage>
               <extent xml:id="extent_5fd1f8e2">16 pages</extent>
               <dimensions unit="cm" xml:id="dimensions_d35d8f70">28 x 23</dimensions>
               <physMedium xml:id="physMedium_ffe79912">Bound in blue cardboard. 48 pages of music paper, flyleaf before the first and after the last music paper. Written in ink. Paper: 12 staves. Paginated 1-17. <lb xml:id="idm73"/>On verso of title page: Mærk: Aaret beregnes fra den 28. Mai / overensstemmende med Tidsregning / af 28de mai 1831 [Sophie's birthday]. / Januar. / Februar. / Marts. / April. / den 9de 1851 Foraaret begynder / [tegning af en engel med bue og pil] (Skytten Himmelt.)<lb xml:id="idm74"/>P. 1: No. 1: Heading: "April. den 10<rend xml:id="idm75" rend="sup">de</rend> (1851) Solskin Foraar". After last bar: dating: "d. 10<rend xml:id="idm76" rend="sup">de</rend> April 51" and Gade's musical signature<lb xml:id="idm77"/>Pages 2-3: No. 2: "April. den 13<rend xml:id="idm78" rend="sup">de</rend> (1851) Ilinger Foraar". After last bar: dating: :13<rend xml:id="idm79" rend="sup">de</rend> April 51" and Gade's musical signature.<lb xml:id="idm80"/>Pages 4-5: No.3. Heading: "April. den 16<rend xml:id="idm81" rend="sup">de</rend> (1851) Klar Himmel Solskin Foraar"<rend xml:id="idm82" fontstyle="italic">.</rend> After last bar: dating: "16 April 51<rend xml:id="idm83" fontstyle="italic">".</rend> and Gade's musical signature.<lb xml:id="idm84"/>
                  <rend xml:id="idm85" fontfam="Arial">Pages 6-16: </rend>These are followed by additions related to the couple’s wedding on 27 April 1852: the hymn-tune “De knælede med Ja mod Ja” [Kneeling they said Yes to each other] and the birth of twins on 20 May 1855: “En Sanger henrykt til sit Hjerte trykker” [An Enchanted Singer Embraces his Beloved Wife] (Henrik Wergeland)  and "Vuggevise" “Min egen stærke Dreng Sang”  ["Lullaby" My own sturdy boy sang] (H.C. Andersen).  However, the marriage lasted only a tragically short time, for on 15 June, 1855, Sophie died. Under these date Gade has drawn a little cross together with the verse: “Herren gav, Herren tog, Hans Navn være lovet i Evighed, Amen!”  [The Lord gave, the Lord took away, His name be praised in all eternity, Amen!]  After a blank page follows the hymn-tune “Enhver som troer og bliver døbt” [Any who believes and is baptized], dated 6 July 1855. The rest of the calendar consists of empty pages of note-paper.</physMedium>
            </physDesc>
